course: dictionary
lesson: 13917
title: When things slowly drain away
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To leach means that water, or something in it, slowly washes or seeps a substance out of another material. Rain can leach minerals out of rock, and it can leach nutrients out of soil. Plants need those nutrients to grow, so the soil becomes poorer.
explain: «Heavy rain leaches goodness from the garden soil.» Heavy rain is water pouring through the ground. The word leaches tells you the goodness is slowly draining away, not vanishing in an instant. Test it: if you swap in "washes out slowly", the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Leach can also be used when something seeps out of an object. «The colour leached out of my red T-shirt in the wash.» The dye did not jump out. It slowly came out over time, and the shirt looked paler afterwards.
fact: Leach is a verb, so its forms are leaches, leached and leaching.
fact: «Leach» means to slowly wash or seep a substance out of something.
fact: Water in soil can leach nutrients, which are the substances plants need to grow.
fact: Chemicals can leach from waste into rivers, and scientists study this to keep water clean.
fact: Do not confuse leach with leech, which is a small animal that sucks blood. The two words sound the same but mean different things.
exercise: «Heavy rain slowly ___ minerals out of the rock.» Which word fits best? | sparkles | *leaches | whistles | climbs
exercise: «The colour leached out of my red T-shirt in the wash.» What does leached mean here? | *Slowly seeped out | Dried in the sun | Ironed flat | Turned into a bigger shirt
exercise: «Chemicals can leach into the river.» What is the chemical doing? | Glowing brightly | Flying into the sky | Freezing solid | *Slowly seeping into the water
test: «The old tea bag leached its brown colour into the hot water.» What does leached mean? | Cooled quickly | Boiled dry | *Slowly seeped out | Was thrown away
test: Which sentence uses leach correctly? | The bird leached a song from the tree. | Leach is the colour of the sky. | *Water can leach minerals from the soil over many years. | The leach ran across the field.
exam: What does leach mean? | Grow tall and strong | Fill up quickly with water | Make a sound like a whistle | *Slowly wash or seep out of something
